    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today leans heavily into favorable platoon splits against mid-tier rotations, led by the day's highest-scoring play, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (73.84). Facing Burnes, **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a massive 14% dynamic platoon boost and a hitter-friendly environment, making him an anchor for R and RBI production. **Isaac Paredes** (70.11) follows closely as a high-floor start, capitalizing on an advantageous matchup against Painter where his ability to exploit platoon splits and his spot in the #3 hole provide significant upside. **James Wood** (65.24) remains an elite volume play; despite a slight park penalty, his xwOBA and lead-off status make him a core driver for our SB-starved roster, while **Gabriel Moreno** (64.45) rounds out the top tier, bolstered by favorable wind conditions and a strong spot in the batting order against Wacha.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley** (58.31), who fell just shy of displacing the lower-ceiling starters. While **Austin Riley** possesses the raw power to swing a week, the optimizer prioritized the higher situational efficiency of **Josh Naylor** (61.53) and **Mickey Moniak** (54.76) due to their platoon advantages and the specific pitching profiles they face tonight. We are exercising caution with **Seiya Suzuki** (45.59), whose score was significantly suppressed by a difficult matchup against the elite arm of Misiorowski; he remains a start only due to a lack of better alternatives in the outfield depth chart today. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Trevor Story** (52.83) situation closely. While his score is bolstered by a 4% bump for stolen base potential against a slower pitcher like Detmers, his struggle against top-tier SP skill creates a variance trap. Similarly, **Zach McKinstry** (42.48) is currently skating at the edge of our efficiency floor; his #9 spot in the order is a major drag on his daily value. We remain without **Corbin Carroll** and **Tyler Soderstrom** due to unavailability, keeping our roster flexibility limited as we chase categories in these final weeks of the season.",
